It is Friday evening.
I am at my home.
The doorbell rings.
I open the door.
My neighbour Asha is standing there.
Her dog, Moti, is with her.
Asha has a heavy bag in her hand.
Moti's food is in it.
She also has Moti's leash.
Moti sees me and wags his tail.
"Maya, thank you very much," Asha says.
"I am going out of town for the weekend."
"You are keeping Moti with you, this is a very big help."
I smile and invite them inside.
"Come in, Asha," I say.
"I really like spending time with Moti."
"This bag is quite heavy," Asha says.
"Put it here on the floor," I say.
Asha puts the bag down.
Our weekend begins now.
